{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And this is the thing that you shall do to them.</b> It would have been fitting to say וזה אשר תעשה להם, as it says immediately afterward, וזה אשר תעשה על המזבח. It added the word הדבר because this section is the section of the offerings, and it alludes to the future: for whoever has no offering may bring דברים (words) and be atoned, in the manner of what is written (Hosea 14:3): ״קחו עמכם דברים״, and it is written (there): ״ונשלמה פרים שפתינו״ — in place of פרים שפתינו." "<b>Take one young bull and two rams.</b> Behold, three — corresponding to the three fathers of the world, Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. <br><b>By way of the Midrash:</b> ״פר אחד בן בקר ואילים שנים״ — this is what is written (Isaiah 46:10): ״מגיד מראשית אחרית״. One bull corresponds to Aaron; two rams correspond to Eleazar and Ithamar — an allusion that the two sons of Aaron are destined to die on account of an offering, and they serve only in two."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:21.983442876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}